- Performance reviews, disciplinary notices, termination notices, HR policies, payroll records, benefits statements.
Financial proof
- Pay stubs, commission reports, bank statements, invoices, tax returns showing lost income or payments.
Work product and deliverables
- Copies of work product, project files, deliverables tied to compensation/dispute.
Witness info
- Names, job titles, contact info for HR staff, supervisors, coworkers, clients who can corroborate your story.
Other
- Any contemporaneous notes you took, photos, calendar entries, meeting invitations, recorded timesheets.
Chain-of-custody and metadata
- Save original files with timestamps and metadata (don’t convert or print until counsel advises). Keep originals where possible.

D — How to preserve electronic evidence (do these now)
- Stop deleting anything relevant. Turn off auto-deletes on email/phone if possible.  
- Export and save copies of emails (preferably .eml or .pst) and text messages (screenshots with timestamps are OK short-term, but native exports are better).  
