Questions to ask Maria Santos (phrasing + why)
1) "What are the exact deadlines I must meet between now and the next court date (responsive pleading, discovery, disclosures)?"  
   - Why: clarifies urgent tasks and avoids default.

2) "Given the case posture, do you recommend we seek additional evidence before the preliminary hearing? If so, what specifically?"  
   - Why: gets her professional view on necessity and value of new evidence.

3) "Which of these records can we obtain quickly by request and which require subpoenas or motions? What are realistic timeframes?"  
   - Why: helps prioritize items you can get immediately vs. those that take weeks.

4) "Who should take the lead on collecting items — me, your office, or do we need court process (subpoena)?"  
   - Why: prevents duplication and missed tasks.

5) "Are any preservation or protective orders needed now to prevent spoliation?"  
   - Why: court can impose sanctions for destroyed evidence; preservation letters/orders can help.

6) "Should we collect written witness statements or affidavits now, or wait until discovery/deposition?"  
   - Why: statements can be useful fast but may affect later credibility or impeachment.

7) "Do we need any expert(s) for damages or technical issues? If yes, when would we engage them and what is the cost/time?"  
   - Why: experts take time and money — need quick decision if their evidence is critical.

8) "What documents do you want me to prioritize sending to you now?"  
   - Why: ensures you provide what counsel actually needs first.

9) "Are there strategic reasons to delay collecting/producing certain materials?"  
   - Why: sometimes timing matters (tactical or privilege issues).

10) "What are the immediate risks if we do not obtain additional evidence before the preliminary hearing?"  
   - Why: helps weigh benefit vs. cost and time.

11) "Will obtaining certain records trigger a need for a protective order (sensitive financial or private info)?"  
   - Why: protects privacy and informs how documents should be produced.

12) "What is the likely scope of discovery in this civil division case and typical timelines in Maricopa County?"  
   - Why: sets expectations for how soon you can compel records.

13) "Do you recommend we try to resolve things before trial (settlement/mediation)? If yes, what evidence strengthens our position in negotiations?"  
   - Why: evidence strategy may differ if aiming to settle.

